# git-crypt: encrypt every file in this directory AT REST.
#
# This is the "{{ encrypted_paths }}" encrypted local area for {{ project_name }}.
# Files committed here are transparently encrypted by git-crypt using the repo's
# symmetric key (kept in {{ password_manager }} + the OS keychain — see
# ../docs/ENCRYPTED_LOCAL_AREAS.md). Locked, the working tree shows ciphertext
# blobs; unlocked, the plaintext. Either way the repo stays safe to push/back up.
#
# `*` routes everything in this subtree through git-crypt's clean/smudge filter.
* filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt

# ...except the plaintext POINTER files, which must stay readable WITHOUT the key
# so the area is self-describing even when locked. `!filter !diff` opts them out.
README.md      !filter !diff
.gitattributes !filter !diff
